1417:Wave 022 completed the runtime-session kernel and narrowed the public app-shell persistence contract: `RuntimeSession` now owns the current `World`/`CommandStack` lifecycle, project/session/autosave use cases consume session methods, and `ProjectSessionPersistenceAdapter` is the only app-shell bridge to `ProjectService` (`architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/implementation-log.md`, “Production files changed”; “DELETE list / proofs”; “Validation-and-preview closure — t1 independent verification”). The same log records residual risks that raw-object accessors remain for active-plane, keyboard/history, selection, rendering-facing consumers, and that `ProjectSessionPersistenceAdapter` still uses private casts from opaque handles (`architecture-audit/cycle-022-runtime-session-kernel-persistence-port-boundary/implementation-log.md`, “Residual risks and next-wave candidates”; “Next-wave recommendation / re-rank”).
1517:Wave 023 completed the runtime-session consumer-port and command-history cleanup: active-plane, selection, keyboard undo/redo, toolbar history, selection deletion, and adapter-local persistence handles now use narrow ports, while raw accessors `worldForUseCases()`, `commandStackForCommandServices()`, `commandStackForShortcuts()`, and reviewer-rejected `commandStackForView()` are absent (`architecture-audit/cycle-023-runtime-session-consumer-ports-command-history-boundary/implementation-log.md`, “Deleted / removed legacy surfaces”; “Consumer-port / command-history closure assessment”). The same implementation log names the remaining central seam: `commandStackForDeferredCommandProducers()` is retained only for deferred canvas/tool/process-history producers, and `worldForView()` remains the separate rendering/view seam (`architecture-audit/cycle-023-runtime-session-consumer-ports-command-history-boundary/implementation-log.md`, “Residual risks and deferred seams”; “Next-wave candidates”).
1706:## Wave 026 — Tool interaction read context and realization adapter seam
1733:The proposals must start with a current inventory of every active `ToolContext.world`, `context.world`, `realize2D(context.world)`, collection-context world, `CanvasViewPort.invokeToolClick`, `createCanvasWorldReadPort(this.world)`, and `createThreeWorldReadPort(this.world)` use. Classify each use by behavior: active-plane/plane lookup, hit-result element lookup, argument collection validation, tool-specific geometric realization, tangent/parallel/perpendicular choice computation, screen-to-3D coordinate support, presentation snapshot, three-scene read model, visibility/read policy, properties/process-tree infeasibility display, and command mutation. The selected design should introduce one or more behavior-sized read/realization contexts, not a renamed `World` facade. If the inventory proves that deleting `ToolContext.world` requires redesigning domain `Element2D.realize2D(world)` / realization ownership broadly, stop and run a reviewed plan-edit mini-cycle rather than hiding a domain-realization wave inside Wave 026.
1745:Lower-priority candidates remain real but are deferred by centrality. Elements visibility is now a named view intent and may later become command-backed, but that would touch command/persistence semantics beyond this tool-read context. Toolbar-history unknown-provider typing, ProjectSessionPersistenceAdapter/ProjectService DTO casts, validation-gate hardening, docs/spec drift, backend/frontend contract stance, Drive/auth, and package/tooling are leaf/enforcement/integration concerns relative to the current raw `World` tool seam. Broad domain realization redesign is more central in concept but too large for a single implementation wave unless the Wave 026 scout proves the narrow tool/read-context deletion is impossible without it.
1786:All Wave 026 validation stdout/stderr must be captured to stable files under the reviewed Cycle 026 implementation directory's `validation/` subdirectory. Undefined commands may be skipped only with exact package-script evidence in the implementation log; defined root or workspace commands are mandatory.
1802:- Canvas and three presentation adapters still depend on domain realization internals. If narrowing them requires changing `Element2D.realize2D(world)` or projection realization ownership broadly, stop for a reviewed plan edit rather than expanding Wave 026.
